        "title": "Format number in thousands separators with jq json cli",
        "body": "<p>Given <code>{&quot;a&quot;: 1234567890}</code>, I want <code>1,234,567,890</code> in the result, how this can be done with jq</p>\n<pre><code>echo '{&quot;a&quot;: 1234567890}' | jq '.a | FORMAT?'\n</code></pre>\n<p>Thanks for <a href=\"https://stackoverflow.com/a/60178790\">@peak's answer</a>, the solution is</p>\n<pre><code>echo '{&quot;a&quot;: 1234567890}' | jq -r 'def h: [while(length&gt;0; .[:-3]) | .[-3:]] | reverse | join(&quot;,&quot;); .a | tostring | h'\n//-&gt; 1,234,567,890\n</code></pre>\n"
      }
